" y=\"125\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\"></image><text x=\"672\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\">Qwen3</text></a>\n      <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-5/\"><image href=\"lecture-1/logos/openai.svg\" x=\"716\" y=\"31\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\"></image><text x=\"716\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"end\">GPT-5</text></a>\n    </g>\n  </svg>\n  <div class=\"model-logo-key\" aria-label=\"Developer logo key\">\n    <span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/openai.svg\" alt=\"\">OpenAI</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/anthropic.svg\" alt=\"\">Anthropic</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/google.svg\" alt=\"\">Google</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/meta.svg\" alt=\"\">Meta</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/xai.svg\" alt=\"\">xAI</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/deepseek.svg\" alt=\"\">DeepSeek</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/qwen.svg\" alt=\"\">Qwen</span><span><img src=\"lecture-1/logos/mistral.svg\" alt=\"\">Mistral</span>\n  </div>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"chart-caption hidden\">\n<p>Selected ECI point estimates from Epoch AI’s <a href=\"https://epoch.ai/data-insights/gpt-4-longest-eci-lead\">benchmarked-model dataset</a>, using releases from March 2023 through August 2025. The graph begins in 2023 because Epoch warns that earlier ECI estimates are sparse and noisy. Confidence intervals overlap for several nearby points, so small vertical differences should not be treated as decisive rankings.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"timeline-key\" aria-label=\"Timeline category legend\" hidden=\"\">\n  <span class=\"model\">Foundation model</span>\n  <span class=\"product\">Product or interface</span>\n  <span class=\"agent\">Agent or tool</span>\n  <span class=\"media\">Media or multimodal</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"timeline-shell\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Selected language-model timeline from 2019 through 2025\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\">\n  <div class=\"timeline-chart\">\n    <div class=\"timeline-years\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2019</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2020</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2021</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2022</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2023</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2024</span><span class=\"timeline-year\">2025</span></div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row openai\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">O</span><strong>OpenAI</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/better-language-models/\"><strong>GPT-2</strong><small>staged release</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/language-models-are-few-shot-learners/\"><strong>GPT-3</strong><small>few-shot</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event product\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/openai-api/\"><strong>API</strong><small>programmable access</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/instruction-following/\"><strong>InstructGPT</strong><small>RLHF</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event product\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/chatgpt/\"><strong>ChatGPT</strong><small>chat interface</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-4-research/\"><strong>GPT-4</strong><small>multimodal input</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/function-calling-and-other-api-updates/\"><strong>Function calling</strong><small>structured tools</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/hello-gpt-4o/\"><strong>GPT-4o</strong><small>real-time multimodal</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/\"><strong>o1</strong><small>reasoning time</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-4o-image-generation/\"><strong>4o image</strong><small>native generation</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event product\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-5/\"><strong>GPT-5 system</strong><small>automatic routing</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row anthropic\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">A</span><strong>Anthropic</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/introducing-claude\"><strong>Claude</strong><small>public launch</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-2\"><strong>Claude 2</strong><small>longer context</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\"><strong>Claude 3</strong><small>Opus · Sonnet · Haiku</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-5-sonnet\"><strong>Claude 3.5</strong><small>coding + Artifacts</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/3-5-models-and-computer-use\"><strong>Computer use</strong><small>GUI action</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/model-context-protocol\"><strong>MCP</strong><small>tools and data</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-7-sonnet\"><strong>Claude 3.7</strong><small>hybrid reasoning</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-4\"><strong>Claude Code</strong><small>coding agent</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-4\"><strong>Claude 4</strong><small>agentic models</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row google\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">G</span><strong>Google</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event product\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/bard-google-ai-search-updates/\"><strong>Bard</strong><small>chat product</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-gemini-ai/\"><strong>Gemini 1.0</strong><small>model family</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/google-gemini-next-generation-model-february-2024/\"><strong>Gemini 1.5</strong><small>long context</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/google-generative-ai-veo-imagen-3/\"><strong>Veo</strong><small>video model</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/google-gemini-ai-update-december-2024/\"><strong>Gemini 2.0</strong><small>agentic era</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-model-thinking-updates-march-2025/\"><strong>Gemini 2.5</strong><small>thinking model</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/generative-media-models-io-2025/\"><strong>Veo 3</strong><small>video + audio</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row meta\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">M</span><strong>Meta</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/large-language-model-llama-meta-ai/\"><strong>LLaMA</strong><small>research release</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-2/\"><strong>Llama 2</strong><small>commercial open weights</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/meta-llama-3/\"><strong>Llama 3</strong><small>stronger open weights</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/meta-llama-3-1/\"><strong>Llama 3.1</strong><small>405B</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-3-2-connect-2024-vision-edge-mobile-devices/\"><strong>Llama 3.2</strong><small>vision + edge</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event media\" href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-4-multimodal-intelligence/\"><strong>Llama 4</strong><small>multimodal MoE</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row xai\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">x</span><strong>xAI</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://x.ai/news/grok\"><strong>Grok</strong><small>first release</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://x.ai/news/grok-2\"><strong>Grok 2</strong><small>second generation</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://x.ai/news/grok-3\"><strong>Grok 3</strong><small>reasoning</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://x.ai/news/grok-4\"><strong>Grok 4</strong><small>next generation</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row deepseek\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">D</span><strong>DeepSeek</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news1226\"><strong>DeepSeek-V3</strong><small>efficient MoE</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news250120/\"><strong>DeepSeek-R1</strong><small>open reasoning weights</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row qwen\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">Q</span><strong>Alibaba · Qwen</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen\"><strong>Qwen-7B</strong><small>open weights</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://qwenlm.github.io/blog/qwen2/\"><strong>Qwen2</strong><small>family expansion</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://qwenlm.github.io/blog/qwen2.5/\"><strong>Qwen2.5</strong><small>multilingual + code</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://qwenlm.github.io/blog/qwen3/\"><strong>Qwen3</strong><small>hybrid thinking</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row china-other\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">中</span><strong>Other China</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event product\" href=\"https://agents.baidu.com/docs/develop/model/ERNIE_bot_introduce/\"><strong>ERNIE Bot</strong><small>Baidu</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12599\"><strong>Kimi k1.5</strong><small>Moonshot</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event agent\" href=\"https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Kimi-K2\"><strong>Kimi K2</strong><small>agentic MoE</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://z.ai/blog/glm-4.5\"><strong>GLM-4.5</strong><small>hybrid reasoning</small></a></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"timeline-row mistral\">\n      <div class=\"timeline-lab\"><span class=\"lab-mark\">Mi</span><strong>Europe · Mistral</strong></div>\n      <div class=\"timeline-events\">\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div><div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://mistral.ai/news/announcing-mistral-7b\"><strong>Mistral 7B</strong><small>open weights</small></a><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://mistral.ai/news/mixtral-of-experts\"><strong>Mixtral</strong><small>mixture of experts</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"><a class=\"timeline-event model\" href=\"https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-2407/\"><strong>Mistral Large 2</strong><small>flagship model</small></a></div>\n        <div class=\"timeline-cell\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"chart-caption hidden\">\n<p>Colored lab marks identify the developer; marker styles identify the kind of release. “Open weights” means model parameters are downloadable under a license. It does not automatically mean that the data, training code, or license satisfies every definition of open source.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Release names are not directly comparable across companies: a “minor” version can be a large capability change, while a new product name may route across several checkpoints. The reliable visual claim is about tempo. Releases that once appeared roughly once or twice a year now arrive as model families, previews, specialist variants, and point updates separated by weeks or days.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-foundational-moments\">The foundational moments</h2>\n<p>A model release earns the name “moment” when it changes a user interface, an engineering workflow, the economics of deployment, or the direction of research—not merely when it moves one leaderboard by a point.</p>\n<div class=\"moment-list\">\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2022-11-30\">Nov 2022</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The ChatGPT moment</strong><p>Instruction following, RLHF, and a frictionless chat product brought general-purpose language models to a mass audience.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2023-02-24\">Feb 2023</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The LLaMA open-weight moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/large-language-model-llama-meta-ai/\">LLaMA</a> was not the first downloadable language model—GPT-J, OPT, and BLOOM came earlier—but its compact research checkpoints catalyzed local fine-tuning and a large family of derivatives.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2023-06-13\">Jun 2023</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The structured tool-use moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://openai.com/index/function-calling-and-other-api-updates/\">Function calling</a> gave applications a dependable JSON interface between a language model and external tools. Earlier systems had already experimented with browsing and acting; this release made the pattern easy to ship through an API.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2023-07-18\">Jul 2023</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The Llama 2 distribution moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-2/\">Llama 2</a> made pretrained and chat-tuned weights available for research and many commercial uses. Its significance was distribution and adaptation—not being the first tool-using model.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2024-02\">Feb 2024</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The long-context moment</strong><p>Gemini 1.5 made a million-token context window a headline capability and shifted attention toward retrieval, memory, and long inputs.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2024-05-13\">May 2024</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The GPT-4o moment</strong><p>Low-latency speech, vision, and text made multimodality feel like one conversation rather than a chain of separate models.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2024-09-12\">Sep 2024</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The o1 moment</strong><p>Inference-time reasoning became a visible product choice: spend more computation after the prompt to improve difficult answers.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2024-11-24\">Nov 2024</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The Cursor moment</strong><p>Composer gained agentic search and terminal use, moving coding assistance from autocomplete toward delegated software work.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2025-01-20\">Jan 2025</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The DeepSeek moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news250120/\">DeepSeek-R1</a> made open-weight reasoning, reinforcement learning, efficient training, and a broader geography of frontier competition impossible to ignore.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2025-02-24\">Feb 2025</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The Claude Code moment</strong><p>A terminal-native coding agent entered research preview, making long-running tool use part of everyday software development.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2025-03-25\">Mar 2025</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The native image moment</strong><p>GPT-4o image generation moved image creation from a separate DALL·E-style model boundary into the conversational model experience.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2025-05-20\">May 2025</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The Veo 3 moment</strong><p>Generated video arrived with native audio, making scene, motion, dialogue, and sound one generation problem.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2025-08-07\">Aug 2025</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The GPT-5 routing moment</strong><p>Users received one interface that automatically chose between a fast model and a deeper reasoning model. The launch system was a router over models—not yet one monolithic network.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2026-01-30\">Jan 2026</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The OpenClaw moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/start/lore\">OpenClaw adopted its current name on 30 January 2026</a>, but the important change was not the rebrand or a new foundation model. Its <a href=\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/concepts/main-session\">self-hosted personal-agent design</a> connected models to messaging channels, a persistent main session, workspace instructions and memory, tools, and background heartbeats. It shifted attention from model weights alone to the agent harness—and to the permissions, identity boundaries, and <a href=\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/gateway/security\">security controls</a> required when an agent can keep acting.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2026-02-05\">Feb 2026</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The Opus 4.6 coding-agent moment</strong><p><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-4-6\">Claude Opus 4.6</a> made longer-running coding tasks and teams of agents headline capabilities. Around the same period, Claude Code creator Boris Cherny <a href=\"https://fortune.com/2026/01/29/100-percent-of-code-at-anthropic-and-openai-is-now-ai-written-boris-cherny-roon/\">said he had not written code by hand since November</a>, and Spotify’s co-CEO <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/12/spotify-says-its-best-developers-havent-written-a-line-of-code-since-december-thanks-to-ai/\">made a similar claim about its best developers</a>. Both accounts describe Claude Code with Opus 4.5, not an effect unique to 4.6; the moment is the workflow shift from typing code to directing and reviewing agents.</p></div></div>\n  <div class=\"moment\"><time class=\"moment-date\" datetime=\"2026-04-07\">Apr 2026</time><div class=\"moment-copy\"><strong>The restricted-release moment</strong><p>Anthropic offered <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/glasswing\">Claude Mythos Preview</a> only to selected cyber-defense partners and said that preview was not planned for general availability. It was not the first withheld model—the GPT-2 episode came years earlier—but it made model access itself a visible capability-dependent product decision.</p></div></div>\n</div>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12948\">DeepSeek-R1 report</a> <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"guo2025deepseekr1\">(DeepSeek-AI 2025)</span> documents the model family’s reinforcement-learning recipe and released distillations.</p>\n<p>Together, these moments trace a progression: <strong>conversation → tools → reasoning → agents → media → persistent personal-agent harnesses → automatic orchestration → capability-dependent access</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-market-follows-the-bottleneck\">The market follows the bottleneck</h2>\n<p>The clearest financial signal of the LLM era was Nvidia. Its GPUs became the scarce general-purpose compute behind both training and inference. Yet the AI trade did not remain a single “GPU stock” story: investor attention moved toward whichever hardware layer appeared scarce next. Use the event windows below to compare those price paths without confusing a quoted share price with company size.</p>\n<div data-ai-market-moments=\"\"></div>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>GPU repricing.</strong> On 25 May 2023, Nvidia shares <a href=\"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nvidia-close-to-becoming-first-trilliondollar-chip-firm-after-stellar-forecast-3090653\">rose 24%</a> after an extraordinary data-center forecast. Its fiscal 2024 data-center revenue later reached $47.5 billion, up 217%, according to its <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581024000029/nvda-20240128.htm\">annual filing</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>The DeepSeek shock.</strong> <a href=\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news250120/\">DeepSeek-R1 launched</a> on 20 January 2025. A week later, fear that more efficient models would require less hardware helped drive a <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/52c54e361616509280bd2775674b6b4b\">16.9% one-day Nvidia decline</a>. That was a change in investor expectations, not proof that compute demand had disappeared. Nvidia later recovered and <a href=\"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nvidia-becomes-first-company-to-clinch-4-trillion-in-market-value-4128409\">reached a $4 trillion market value</a> in July 2025.</li>\n<li><strong>The bottleneck expands.</strong> AI systems need more than accelerators. High-bandwidth memory feeds model weights and activations to GPUs; <a href=\"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/micron-set-for-record-high-after-ai-demand-steers-strong-forecast-surprise-profit-3347470\">Micron said</a> its 2024 HBM capacity was sold out, and <a href=\"https://news.skhynix.com/en/sk-hynix-announces-4q24-financial-results/\">SK hynix reported</a> that HBM exceeded 40% of Q4 2024 DRAM revenue. CPUs coordinate storage, networking, retrieval, tool calls, and high-volume inference. By July 2026, <a href=\"https://newsroom.intel.com/corporate/intel-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results\">Intel reported</a> stronger demand while <a href=\"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/intel-sales-profit-forecast-beat-estimates-boosts-spending-plans-on-ai-boom-4809863\">industry reporting</a> linked part of the CPU shortage to agentic workloads. These gains were specific to changing bottlenecks; they did not lift every hardware producer equally or prove that one workload single-handedly revived a company.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The economic lesson is that markets repeatedly try to identify the next scarce input. The technical lesson is similar: optimize the bottleneck that limits the whole system, not the component with the loudest story.</p>\n<h2 id=\"beyond-text-vlms-multimodality-and-action\">Beyond text: VLMs, multimodality, and action</h2>\n<p>The output distinguishes several model interfaces. An <strong>LLM</strong> maps text tokens to text tokens, as in the dialogue examples earlier in the lecture. Vision-language, multimodal, and action models extend that interface in different directions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"vlm-ground-an-image\">VLM: ground an image</h3>\n<p>A <strong>vision-language model (VLM)</strong> can connect a text instruction to visual evidence. In the example below, the input is a street photograph plus the instruction “Locate the bus and people.” The output grounds those words in regions of the image rather than returning only a sentence.</p>\n<figure class=\"model-example vision-grounding-example\">\n  <div class=\"vision-grounding-grid\">\n    <div class=\"vision-grounding-panel\">\n      <strong>Image input</strong>\n      <img src=\"lecture-1/vlm-street-scene.jpg\" alt=\"A city bus with several people walking in front of it on a street in Madrid.\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"vision-grounding-panel\">\n      <strong>Grounded output</strong>\n      <div class=\"vision-scene\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The same street photograph with one bounding box around the bus and three bounding boxes around people.\">\n        <img src=\"lecture-1/vlm-street-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n        <span class=\"vision-box vision-box--bus\"><b>bus</b></span>\n        <span class=\"vision-box vision-box--person-a\"><b>person</b></span>\n        <span class=\"vision-box vision-box--person-b\"><b>person</b></span>\n        <span class=\"vision-box vision-box--person-c\"><b>person</b></span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>Illustrative grounding output on a real street photograph from the <a href=\"https://github.com/ultralytics/assets/blob/main/im/bus.jpg\">Ultralytics example assets</a>. Bounding boxes make the connection between a word and an image region explicit.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h3 id=\"multimodal-model-summarize-a-video\">Multimodal model: summarize a video</h3>\n<p>A multimodal model can combine evidence across time and return another medium. Here the input is a five-second video; the example output is a text summary of the full sequence.</p>\n<figure class=\"model-example multimodal-video-example\">\n  <div class=\"model-example-grid\">\n    <div>\n      <strong class=\"model-example-label\">Video input</strong>\n      <video autoplay=\"\" muted=\"\" loop=\"\" playsinline=\"\" controls=\"\" preload=\"auto\" poster=\"lecture-1/multimodal-flower-poster.jpg\" aria-label=\"A close-up time-lapse video of a red flower opening from a bud.\">\n        <source src=\"lecture-1/multimodal-flower.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n        Your browser does not support embedded video.\n      </video>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"model-example-output\">\n      <strong>Text output</strong>\n      <p>“A close-up time-lapse shows a red flower opening from a closed bud.”</p>\n      <small>The change is visible only across the sequence: the first frame shows the bud, while later frames show the open flower.</small>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>Five-second CC0 sample video from <a href=\"https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4\">MDN Web Docs</a>. The clip autoplays muted and remains controllable.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h3 id=\"vla-turn-perception-into-action\">VLA: turn perception into action</h3>\n<p>A <strong>vision-language-action model (VLA)</strong> extends the prediction target. Instead of ending with a sentence, the system must produce an action that changes the physical world:</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">camera frames</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">instruction</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">robot state</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n(\\text{camera frames},\\ \\text{instruction},\\ \\text{robot state})\n\\longrightarrow\n(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_T).\n</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<figure class=\"model-example vla-video-example\">\n  <div class=\"model-example-grid\">\n    <div>\n      <strong class=\"model-example-label\">Camera input and task</strong>\n      <div class=\"video-embed\">\n        <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/7Q-FHj2r4NU?autoplay=1&amp;mute=1&amp;playsinline=1&amp;loop=1&amp;playlist=7Q-FHj2r4NU&amp;rel=0\" title=\"Robohand autonomously throwing away trash\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"model-example-output\">\n      <strong>Action output</strong>\n      <p>The system turns camera observations and the disposal task into a sequence of robot commands that moves the hand, grasps the trash, and discards it.</p>\n      <small>Unlike a caption, the output changes the environment and must be evaluated for physical success and safety.</small>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Q-FHj2r4NU\">Robohand finally throwing away the trash autonomously</a>, a hackathon demonstration by Alexan Hayrapetyan.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><a href=\"https://deepmind.google/blog/rt-2-new-model-translates-vision-and-language-into-action/\">RT-2</a> <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"zitkovich2023rt2\">(<span class=\"nocase\">Zitkovich et al.</span> 2023)</span> showed how web-scale vision-language knowledge could transfer into robotic control. <a href=\"https://github.com/openvla/openvla\">OpenVLA</a> <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"kim2024openvla\">(<span class=\"nocase\">Kim et al.</span> 2024)</span> later released a 7B open vision-language-action model trained on robot demonstrations. The promise is transfer: an instruction such as “move the can near the matching color” can draw on concepts learned outside a narrow robot dataset. The difficulty is that wrong physical actions have costs that wrong sentences do not.</p>\n<h3 id=\"specialization-is-another-axis-of-progress\">Specialization is another axis of progress</h3>\n<p>The same adaptation recipe used for Armenian can target a historical language such as Old English:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>inspect whether the tokenizer fragments the language excessively;</li>\n<li>assemble and document a clean, licensed corpus;</li>\n<li>continue pre-training a suitable base model;</li>\n<li>instruction-tune on translation, morphology, retrieval, or annotation tasks; and</li>\n<li>evaluate on held-out texts with domain experts, not only with an automatic modern-language metric.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The research question is not “Can a giant model produce something that looks old?” It is whether the model preserves morphology, meaning, uncertainty, and source evidence on material it did not memorize. Recent <a href=\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.loreslm-1.21/\">low-resource language-model research</a> explores this continued-training route for historical languages.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-remember\">What to remember</h2>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>ChatGPT changed the interface more than the underlying definition of NLP.</strong> Many tasks became instructions inside one dialogue system.</li>\n<li><strong>RLHF learns preferences, not truth.</strong> Demonstrations, rankings, a reward model, and policy optimization can improve behavior while introducing new failure modes.</li>\n<li><strong>A benchmark score belongs to a protocol.</strong> Checkpoint identity, prompts, tools, graders, and uncertainty matter as much as the headline number.</li>\n<li><strong>The Llama 4 controversy was a reproducibility lesson.</strong> An experimental chat variant and the public checkpoint were not interchangeable; that does not imply every result was fake.</li>\n<li><strong>The model frontier is global but uneven.</strong> The United States and China lead frontier-scale development, while regional ecosystems create value through sovereignty, deployment, openness, and language coverage.</li>\n<li><strong>Capability shifts move engineering and economic bottlenecks.</strong> Chat, reasoning, agents, native media, and routing changed how models were used, while demand moved across accelerators, memory, and infrastructure.</li>\n<li><strong>Multimodal interfaces differ by their outputs.</strong> VLMs can ground language in image regions, multimodal systems can interpret sequences such as video, and VLAs produce actions that change the physical world.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 class=\"unnumbered\" id=\"references\">References</h2>\n<div id=\"refs\" class=\"references csl-bib-body hanging-indent\" role=\"list\">\n<div id=\"ref-chen2021humaneval\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\n<span class=\"nocase\">Chen, Mark, Jerry Tworek, Heewoo Jun, et al.</span> 2021. <span>“Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2107.03374</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.03374\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.03374</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-chiang2024chatbotarena\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nChiang, Wei-Lin, Lianmin Zheng, Ying Sheng, et al. 2024. <span>“Chatbot Arena: An Open Platform for Evaluating <span>LLM</span>s by Human Preference.”</span> <em>Proceedings of the 41st International Conference on Machine Learning</em>. <a href=\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/chiang24b.html\">https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/chiang24b.html</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-cobbe2021gsm8k\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nCobbe, Karl, Vineet Kosaraju, Mohammad Bavarian, et al. 2021. <span>“Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2110.14168</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14168\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14168</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-guo2025deepseekr1\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nDeepSeek-AI. 2025. <span>“<span>DeepSeek-R1</span>: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in <span>LLM</span>s via Reinforcement Learning.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2501.12948</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12948\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12948</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-hendrycks2021mmlu\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nHendrycks, Dan, Collin Burns, Steven Basart, et al. 2021. <span>“Measuring Massive Multitask Language Understanding.”</span> <em>International Conference on Learning Representations</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03300\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03300</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-hendrycks2021math\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nHendrycks, Dan, Collin Burns, Saurav Kadavath, et al. 2021. <span>“Measuring Mathematical Problem Solving with the <span>MATH</span> Dataset.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2103.03874</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.03874\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.03874</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-kim2024openvla\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\n<span class=\"nocase\">Kim, Moo Jin, Karl Pertsch, Siddharth Karamcheti, et al.</span> 2024. <span>“<span>OpenVLA</span>: An Open-Source Vision-Language-Action Model.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2406.09246</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09246\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09246</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-ouyang2022instructgpt\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\n<span class=\"nocase\">Ouyang, Long, Jeff Wu, Xu Jiang, et al.</span> 2022. <span>“Training Language Models to Follow Instructions with Human Feedback.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2203.02155</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02155\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02155</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-rein2023gpqa\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nRein, David, Betty Li Hou, Asa Cooper Stickland, et al. 2023. <span>“<span>GPQA</span>: A Graduate-Level Google-Proof <span>Q&amp;A</span> Benchmark.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2311.12022</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12022\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12022</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-wang2023faireval\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nWang, Peiyi, Lei Li, Liang Chen, et al. 2023. <span>“Large Language Models Are Not Fair Evaluators.”</span> <em>arXiv Preprint arXiv:2305.17926</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17926\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17926</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-wang2023selfconsistency\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\nWang, Xuezhi, Jason Wei, Dale Schuurmans, et al. 2023. <span>“Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models.”</span> <em>International Conference on Learning Representations</em>. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11171\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11171</a>.\n</div>\n<div id=\"ref-zitkovich2023rt2\" class=\"csl-entry\" role=\"listitem\">\n<span class=\"nocase\">Zitkovich, Brianna, Tianhe Yu, Sichun Xu, et al.</span> 2023. <span>“<span>RT-2</span>: Vision-Language-Action Models Transfer Web Knowledge to Robotic Control.”</span> <em>Proceedings of the 7th Conference on Robot Learning</em>. <a href=\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v229/zitkovich23a.html\">https://proceedings.mlr.press/v229/zitkovich23a.html</a>.\n</div>\n</div>";
